6045487 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417319 1071 "Which statement is equivalent to $(A∧C)∨B?$" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417319 1072 #uuid "64b80180-617d-5ce8-ba15-27c7480d01c0" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417319 1074 "We distribute the disjunction over the conjunction, as follows:\n\n$$\n(A∧C)∨B≡(A∨B)∧(C∨B)\n$$\n\nNow, since $C∨B≡B∨C,$ we can write\n\n$$\n(A∨B)∧(C∨B)≡(A∨B)∧(B∨C).\n$$" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417320 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417312 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417320 1069 "q-81600" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417320 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417320 1071 "Which statement is equivalent to $¬A∧(C∨B)?$" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417320 1072 #uuid "702e0bd2-2647-576e-a4be-58f40f9e69a7" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417320 1074 "We distribute the conjunction over the disjunction, as follows:\n\n$$\n¬A∧(C∨B)≡(¬A∧C)∨(¬A∧B)\n$$\n\nNow, since $¬A∧C≡C∧¬A,$ we can write\n\n$$\n(¬A∧C)∨(¬A∧B)≡(C∧¬A)∨(¬A∧B).\n$$" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417321 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417301 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417321 1069 "q-128645" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417321 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417321 1071 "Which statement is equivalent to $(A∧C)∨(B∧A)?$" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417321 1072 #uuid "87910bfb-c2b0-56bd-8dea-41292afab3d9" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417321 1074 "First,  since $A∨C≡C∨A,$ we can write\n\n$$\n(A∧C)∨(B∧A)≡(C∧A)∨(B∧A).\n$$\n\nThen,  we can factor out the conjunction with $A,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n(C∧A)∨(B∧A)≡(C∨B)∧A\n$$" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417322 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417309 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417322 1069 "q-128637" 13194139534282 17592186045417 true] [17592186417322 1070 #edb/ref 175